# wuko-plugin-{{NS}}

An SDK-backed Wuko plugin with a shared `{{NS}}_slug` helper. Resolve the pinned SDK and run the native Go checks directly:

```sh
go mod tidy
go fmt ./...
go vet ./...
go test ./...
go build -o wuko-plugin-{{NS}} .
```

The executable keeps stdin/stdout exclusively for protocol frames; diagnostics go to stderr. Start and Stop are command-wide hooks. Edit lifecycle.go to use values from plugins.{{NS}}.with.

The scaffold targets [plugin protocol v4](https://github.com/up2jj/wuko/blob/main/docs/plugin-protocol-v4.md) through `github.com/up2jj/wuko/plugin/sdk`. The SDK owns the concurrent JSONL transport, cancellation, declarations, and plugin-to-host callbacks. Step handlers receive phase-specific `sdk.ValidateRequest`, `sdk.RunRequest`, `sdk.ServiceRequest`, or `sdk.CleanupRequest` values. Validation and run handlers use their request's `Host` after declaring each required capability with `sdk.WithHostCallbacks`; undeclared calls are rejected locally. `Host.Secret` requires `sdk.HostFunctionCall`.

Executor output is streamed in bounded SDK events and captured according to Wuko's output policy. A transport-safe aggregate ceiling prevents a captured result from exceeding the 10 MiB protocol frame limit. The generated go.mod pins the SDK to the Wuko release that created this project.

The generated `wuko.release.yaml` runs the tests and the SDK-aware release helper, which cross-compiles deterministic Darwin/Linux archives for amd64/arm64 and generates `plugin.json`. From a marketplace repository, build and publish in one command:

```sh
wuko marketplace plugin release --version 0.1.0 --description "Describe the plugin" ../wuko-plugin-{{NS}}
```

Wuko runs the workflow with the plugin project as its working directory, reads its `bundle` output, and verifies the manifest and every declared archive before updating the catalog.

Consuming workflows must declare this plugin's manifest source. Run `wuko plugin lock FILE` to
create `wuko.lock` beside the workflow, commit both files, and use `wuko run --file FILE --frozen-lockfile` in CI. Local bundle paths are relative to the workflow;
after rebuilding, refresh the pin with `wuko plugin lock FILE --update`. Remote workflow runs
fetch current plugin manifests and reuse verified archives without touching local lockfiles.
